Goal also wants route_sequence_context_set ?candidate (but not explicitly in goal). However some clearance actions set route_sequence_context_set as effect (origin_loaded, destination_loaded, full_load). The nominal clearance does NOT set route_sequence_context_set. Goal does not require route_sequence_context_set, but many later actions (like attach_service_window, validate_route_sequence) require it. However goal does not require those. So we can use nominal clearance which does not set route_sequence_context_set. However goal also wants candidate_finalized shift_candidate_beta. To finalize, we need either finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation (requires compliance_validation_complete ?candidate and not candidate_finalized) OR finalize_candidate_direct (requires candidate_clearance_established ?candidate, not route_sequence_context_set ?candidate, not candidate_finalized) OR finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation (requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_validated, not candidate_finalized). Since we may not have route_sequence_validated, we can use finalize_candidate_direct after clearance (nominal) which does not set route_sequence_context_set, satisfying precondition not route_sequence_context_set ?candidate. Also finalize_candidate_direct adds candidate_finalized and dispatch_ready.

