But note stage_schedule_candidate also requires not origin_leg_loaded ?transport_leg. Since we haven't loaded origin leg yet (we will not load origin leg; we only load container onto leg, not origin leg loaded). However origin_leg_loaded refers to whether origin leg is loaded (i.e., cargo loaded onto transport leg at origin?). Actually origin_leg_loaded is a predicate that indicates the transport leg is loaded at origin? There's also destination_leg_loaded. The assemble actions can set origin_leg_loaded or destination_leg_loaded depending on which assemble action used. We plan to use assemble_transport_leg (which does not set either loaded). So origin_leg_loaded and destination_leg_loaded will be false after assembly. Good.

Thus stage_schedule_candidate precondition not origin_leg_loaded holds.

After staging, we can verify loading profile (nominal or destination flag) to get candidate_loading_verified. There are two verify actions: verify_loading_profile_nominal and verify_loading_profile_destination_flag. Both require candidate_staged_for_loading, candidate_skill_certificate_linked, candidate_operator_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, plus either not destination_leg_loaded (nominal) or destination_leg_loaded (destination flag). Since we have not loaded destination leg (we only loaded container onto leg, not destination leg loaded). So we can use verify_loading_profile_nominal (requires not destination_leg_loaded). That will give candidate_loading_verified.

Thus flow for beta:

- Ensure candidate_prepared beta (need vehicle_allocated, task_profile_linked).
- Assign operator, skill certificate, compliance certificate (after release from alpha).
- Assemble transport leg (using origin lock etc).
- Authorize loading.
- Load container onto leg (using beta as candidate).
- Stage schedule candidate.
- Verify loading profile nominal => candidate_loading_verified.
- Establish clearance nominal => candidate_clearance_established (also requires candidate_loading_verified, compliance certificate linked, loading container linked, loading container leg linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not destination_leg_loaded).
- Finalize candidate direct => candidate_finalized, dispatch_ready.
- Allocate dispatch slot for beta.
- Execute dispatch for beta (dispatched).

Now for origin and destination availability:

We need to make them dispatch_ready, allocate dispatch slot, dispatch.

Preconditions for mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready: origin_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not dispatch_ready ?origin_availability.

